@echo off
cd /d "C:\Users\SubratoBiswas\trinamix-conversion-workbench"
echo Cleaning any git locks...
del /f /q ".git\index.lock" 2>nul
del /f /q ".git\HEAD.lock" 2>nul
echo Dropping tracked bytecode...
git rm -r --cached --ignore-unmatch backend/app/__pycache__ backend/app/services/__pycache__ backend/app/parsers/__pycache__
echo Staging...
git add -A
echo Committing (no-op if clean)...
git commit -m "FIX: rejected mappings no longer write their source column into the FBDI. Reported: reject a suggested mapping, the UI and the downloaded mapping CSV both say 'rejected', but the generated FBDI still carried values from that rejected column. ROOT CAUSE in build_converted_dataframe/_transform_frame: the per-target dedup ranks rejected(1) above suggested(0), so a rejected row correctly WINS and becomes the field's mapping - but the only skip was for not_applicable, and 'rejected' merely suppressed the suggested_transformation (status != 'rejected' on the rules line) while has_src stayed true, so the rejected column's values were still emitted. FIX: a discarded status (not_applicable OR rejected) never reads source_column - has_src now requires 'not _discarded' - and such a mapping is skipped entirely unless an explicit default_value was attached, in which case that default is emitted as a CONSTANT (preserves Invoice Match Option = Receipt). Verified with the real _transform_frame: approved keeps its source, rejected emits no column, rejected+default emits the constant, not_applicable still skipped, and the rejected column's values no longer appear anywhere. Works for EXISTING rejections too: this is a generate-time fix that reads the stored status, apply_learned _eligible() never re-applies a 'rejected' row (suggested, or approved under force, only), and the dedup keeps rejected above a stale suggested row - so previously-rejected mappings are honoured on the next Generate with no re-mapping. Also bundles the upload durable-copy logging hardening."
echo Pushing...
git push origin main
echo.
echo ====== DONE - Press any key to close ======
pause
